==============================================================================
SS4  Why no finite check can settle (STAR) -- an explicit construction
==============================================================================

  PROPOSITION (proved by construction; the algebra is verified exactly
  below).  For every X there are sequences lambda+ , lambda- : N ->
  {+1,-1} with lambda+-(n) = lambda(n) for ALL n <= X and
      S+(x)/x -> +0.248...   and   S-(x)/x -> -0.248... ,
  while S(x)/x -> 0 must hold if (STAR) is true.  Hence 'S(x) = o(x)'
  is not a finite-prefix property: any computation that inspects only
  n <= X returns LITERALLY THE SAME DATA for lambda, lambda+ and
  lambda-, so no such computation can decide (STAR).

  CONSTRUCTION.  Let A be a set of integers with minimum gap >= 3 (use
  A subset of {n : 4 | n}) and put lambda'(n) = -lambda(n) for n in A,
  lambda'(n) = lambda(n) otherwise.  Flipping lambda at n changes the
  correlation summand at index n (term lambda(n)lambda(n+2)) and at
  index n-2 (term lambda(n-2)lambda(n)); gap >= 3 makes these pairs
  disjoint, so with f(n) = lambda(n)lambda(n+2),
      S'(x) - S(x) = -2 * [ sum_{n in A, n<=x} f(n)
                            + sum_{n in A, n<=x+2} f(n-2) ].
  Choose A = A+ := { n > X+2, 4 | n, f(n) = f(n-2) = -1 }: then every
  term in brackets equals -1 and
      S+(x) - S(x) = 4*#{n in A+ : n <= x} + 2*eps,  eps in {0,1},
  which grows like (#A+/x)*4*x.  The mirror choice
      A- := { n > X+2, 4 | n, f(n) = f(n-2) = +1 }
  gives S-(x) - S(x) = -4*#{n in A- : n <= x} - 2*eps.
  The sets use the TRUE values of f at indices n > X+2 only; on the
  prefix [1,X] the sequences are identical, by construction.
  As a control, the 'naive' choice A0 = {n > X, 4 | n} (flip every
  multiple of 4) is also computed: it is NOT a witness, which is worth
  recording -- Liouville correlations resist naive arithmetic tampering.

  X = 10000, exact computation up to x = 10000000 (f and S are integer).

  (a) PREFIX AGREEMENT (the whole point):
[PASS] S4.prefix.identical   |  lambda, lambda+ and lambda- agree on every n <= 10000 (0 differences); the first index in A+ or A- is n = 10012
[PASS] S4.prefix.sums.identical   |  and the correlation partial sums agree EXACTLY for every x <= 10000: S(x) = S+(x) = S-(x) there
[PASS] S4.identity.exact   |  the identity S+-(x) - S(x) = +/-4*#{n in A+- : n <= x} +/- 2*eps (eps in {0,1}) holds EXACTLY at every x <= 10000000

